{"id":"NCT01351545","title":"A Multicenter Access and Distribution Protocol for Unlicensed Cryopreserved Cord Blood Units (CBUs)","official":"A Multicenter Access and Distribution Protocol for Unlicensed Cryopreserved Cord Blood Units (CBUs) for Transplantation in Pediatric and Adult Patients With Hematologic Malignancies and Other Indications","summary":"This study is an access and distribution protocol for unlicensed cryopreserved cord blood units (CBUs) in pediatric and adult patients with hematologic malignancies and other indications.","conditions":["Hematologic Malignancies","Inherited Disorders of Metabolism","Inherited Abnormalities of Platelets","Histiocytic Disorders","Acute Myelogenous Leukemia (AML or ANLL)","Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (ALL)","Other Acute Leukemia","Chronic Myelogenous Leukemia (CML)","Myelodysplastic (MDS) / Myeloproliferative (MPN) Diseases","Other Leukemia","Hodgkin Lymphoma","Non-hodgkin Lymphoma","Multiple Myeloma/ Plasma Cell Disorder (PCD)","Inherited Abnormalities of Erythrocyte Differentiation or Function","Disorders of the Immune System","Autoimmune Diseases","Severe Aplastic Anemia"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"A multicenter access and distribution protocol for unlicensed cryopreserved cord blood units (CBUs)"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Disorders affecting the hematopoietic system that are inherited, acquired, or result from myeloablative treatment\n* Signed informed consent (and signed assent, if applicable) obtained prior to study enrollment\n* Pediatric and adult patients of any age\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Patients who are receiving only licensed CBUs\n* Cord blood transplant recipients at international transplant centers\n* Patients who are enrolled on another IND protocol to access the unlicensed CBU(s)\n* Patients whose selected unlicensed CBU(s) will be more than minimally manipulated","minAge":"","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":99999,"start":"2011-10","pcd":"2041-10","upd":"2026-07-06","sponsor":"Center for International Blood and Marrow Transplant Research","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Elizabeth Fosberg, B.A. · 10-CBA@ndmp.org"],"sites":[{"f":"University of Alabama at Birmingham","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35233","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"Joseph Chewning, MD · jchewning@peds.uab.edu"},{"f":"Banner MD Anderson Cancer Center","city":"Gilbert","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85234","s":"R","lat":33.3528,"lon":-111.789,"c":"Matthew Ulrickson, MD · 480-256-3223 · Matthew.Ulrickson@bannerhealth.com"},{"f":"Phoenix Children's Hospital","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85016","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":"Dana Salzberg, MD · 602-546-0920 · dsalzberg@phoenixchildrens.com"},{"f":"Mayo Clinic Arizona (adults)","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85054","s":"STOP","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":""},{"f":"University of Arizona Medical Center - Tucson","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85224","s":"R","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":"Emmanuel Katsanis, MD · katsanis@peds.arizona.edu"},{"f":"Arkansas Children's Hospital","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72202","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"Jason Farrar, MD · JEFarrar@uams.edu"},{"f":"City of Hope","city":"Duarte","pr":"California","zip":"91010","s":"R","lat":34.1394,"lon":-117.9773,"c":"Monzr Al Malki, MD · malmalki@coh.org"},{"f":"Children's Hospital of Los Angeles","city":"Glendale","pr":"California","zip":"91204","s":"R","lat":34.1425,"lon":-118.2551,"c":"Neena Kapoor, MD · nkapoor@chla.usc.edu"},{"f":"Scripps Green Hospital","city":"La Jolla","pr":"California","zip":"92037","s":"R","lat":32.8473,"lon":-117.2742,"c":"James R Mason, MD · mason.james@scrippshealth.org"},{"f":"University of California San Diego","city":"La Jolla","pr":"California","zip":"92093","s":"R","lat":32.8473,"lon":-117.2742,"c":"Kaitlyn Dykes, MD · 8588226600 · kcdykes@health.ucsd.edu"},{"f":"Loma Linda 